# Solo Dev Hub — global AI rules

Managed by Solo Dev Hub: formats and contracts shared by every project. Per-project context (name, repos, microservices) is in the repo's own `CLAUDE.md`.

## How the rules apply

- **A repo's own `CLAUDE.md` wins.** Where it conflicts with this section or a skill, follow the repo and name the conflict to the owner in one line.
- **A step that has a skill starts by invoking that skill in the same turn.** Skills change between sessions. Not a source: skill text re-injected after a compaction, a compaction summary, memory, or the previous release's artifact ("how it was done last time").
- **A procedure the owner can choose is a default, not a duty.** Who fixes review findings, who closes, how much ceremony — the owner decides per release; a skill only supplies the default.
- **Stop what you started.** Before finishing a task, stop the processes you launched — dev servers, watchers, test runners, background shells. Anything left running on purpose: name it and why.

